From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:08:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: regulator: qcom,usb-vbus-regulator: add PMI8998

The PMI8998 OTG block has the same register layout as the PM8150B one,
but its current-limit selector uses 250 mA steps from 250 mA to 2 A, so
it cannot use qcom,pm8150b-vbus-reg as a fallback compatible.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 .../bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml          | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml
index 024b34d0eb..a26cbef30d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@ description: |
   The pm8150b variant uses an OTG current-limit selector, supporting limits
   of 500 mA, 1000 mA, 1500 mA, 2000 mA, 2500 mA and 3000 mA.
 
+  The pmi8998 variant has the same register layout as pm8150b, but its OTG
+  current-limit selector uses 250 mA steps from 250 mA to 2000 mA.
+
   The pm4125 variant uses a different register layout with a 2-bit VBOOST
   voltage selector supporting output voltages of 4.25 V, 4.5 V, 4.75 V
   and 5.0 V.
@@ -27,6 +30,7 @@ properties:
       - enum:
           - qcom,pm8150b-vbus-reg
           - qcom,pm4125-vbus-reg
+          - qcom,pmi8998-vbus-reg
       - items:
           - enum:
               - qcom,pm6150-vbus-reg
@@ -49,6 +53,7 @@ allOf:
               - qcom,pm6150-vbus-reg
               - qcom,pm7250b-vbus-reg
               - qcom,pmi632-vbus-reg
+              - qcom,pmi8998-vbus-reg
     then:
       required:
         - regulator-min-microamp
